action.prompt:
Use case: stylized-concept. Asset type: production animation sprite sheet for the existing 2D side-scroller Magic Drink.
Reference images: the existing Hexy ribbon-swing sheet and stand-fire sheet define EXACT character identity, clothing, proportions, clean shaded cartoon/anime game illustration, and which hand holds her yellow star wand. NEW ANIMATION required; the previous sheet is too stiff because only an arm moves.
Create a transparent 4 columns by 4 rows sprite sheet: exactly SIXTEEN separated full-body Hexy drawings, every cel facing RIGHT, same character scale in each cel, generous clear gutters. No text, guides, frame borders, numbers, backdrop or ground shadows. Render at large resolution. True transparent alpha.
Character: petite chibi witch, huge pink flowing hair, navy pointed floppy witch hat with yellow star, white short sleeve sailor shirt, red neck bow, navy pleated skirt with sensible coverage, dark socks, big black shoes with gold buckles. Keep her original head/body proportions. NO redesign. She holds the SHORT gold star wand consistently in the FAR hand (the forward/right-side arm when facing right in the reference). The near free arm counterbalances. Keep full hat, boots and wand visible in EVERY cell. No ribbons, magical trails or effects baked onto the character.
Animate the WHOLE BODY: clear bending knees, changing foot support, torso compression and twist, whipping pink hair, hat follow-through, lively determined facial acting. Feet may spread and pivot but never change character size. This is an energetic cartoon whip attack animation sheet, not sixteen standing poses.
Read left to right top to bottom:
ROW 1, basic forward whip, four key poses: (1) low crouched windup, weight on back bent leg, torso twists back, wand cocked over shoulder; (2) explosive forward step, front knee bent and rear heel lifted, torso leaning strongly forward and wand arm driving diagonally down toward target at right; (3) deep forward lunge follow-through, star wand extended right at waist/chest height, hair streaming back, free arm trailing; (4) recoil with weight shifting back, head and shoulders still leaning right, wand finishing across front.
ROW 2, return/backhand whip, four key poses: (5) feet pivot, hips twist away from viewer into a three-quarter-back posture while HEAD still looks to the RIGHT, far wand hand drawn LOW across body; (6) rising diagonal backhand cut from low to high toward RIGHT, shoulders rotate, bent rear leg pushes; (7) twisting follow-through with wand HIGH forward-right, one heel lifted, hair swings forward then curls back; (8) balanced ready stance with bent knees and lower wand, settles to return to row1.
ROWS 3 and 4, eight phases of a DISTINCT HEAVY OVERHEAD SLAM:
(9) deep low anticipation, hips back, wand pulled behind head;
(10) extend legs and arch chest, star wand high above and slightly behind head;
(11) strongest high overhead stretch with raised rear heel, clear S-shaped action line, free hand forward for balance;
(12) begin downward strike, torso folding forward, wand arm sweeping down overhead;
(13) IMPACT pose: deep planted front-knee lunge, upper body bent forcefully forward, star wand thrust down-right close to knee height, rear leg stretched, hair kicked upward from momentum;
(14) follow-through low crouch with wand pointing forward/down and hair spilling forward;
(15) recover lifting torso and pulling wand inward, knees still bent;
(16) ready stance facing right, wand held low forward, hair settling.
Major pose silhouette changes should make this feel satisfying in a beat-em-up. Emphasize real anatomical articulation; do not merely rotate or translate the same static doll. Same canonical hand across all 16 drawings. All drawings must stay inside individual equal cells with empty gaps.
